58.steps:
1. Make sure there are multiple WAN interfaces configured(at least two WAN interfaces configured, eg. X3 is the primary WAN), and X1 is non primary WAN;

2. Add proper address objects of host type and range type, also add group object with several address objects included as its members;

3. Select another interface, configure it as Transparent mode member interface;

4. Run some basic traffic(eg, http(s)/ping/FTP, and mail related), make sure WAN side users can visit services deployed in Transparent range servers;

5. Retest 'step 4', initiate similar traffic from X1 WAN subnet hosts(make sure proper NAT policy already added)

63.steps:
1. Navigate to Match Objects/Addresses page, create two Address Object(eg. named 'DMZ Host 1', 'DMZ Host 2') with DMZ selected for 'Zone Assignment', fill in proper IP address belonged to WAN subnet;
2. Create an Address Object(eg. named 'DMZ Range') with DMZ selected for 'Zone Assignment', fill in proper IP address range belonged to WAN subnet;
3. Create an Address Group(eg. named 'DMZ Host Group'), add 'DMZ Host 1' and 'DMZ Host 2' to In Group list;
4. Navigate to System/Interfaces page, select an unassigned interface(eg. X3) by clicking Edit icon button, select 'DMZ' for Zone type, 'Transparent IP Mode(Splice L3 Subnet)' for Mode/IP assignment, verify all the address object/group created in Step 1 ~ Step 3, select one of them for 'Transparent Range' and save the settings;
5. Set 'Zone Assignment' as LAN/WAN/Custom type, retest above steps;

67.steps:
1. Configure primary WAN interface with non-24 subnet(eg. 10.61.134.125/255.255.255.248), add several host/range AO belong to this subnet, add a group AO with these host/range AOs included;

2. Add several host/range AO out of this subnet, add a group AO with these host/range AOs included;

3. Clear settings in above steps, retest with 28 bit network length configured;

4. Clear settings in above steps, retest with 30 bit network length configured;

GEN7-28861.steps:
1. Unassign default WAN interface X1;

2. Select another interface(eg. interface X18 for X86 platform), configure it as WAN interface with static IP, proper subnet mask(proper DNS server IPs are also needed);

3. Add several host object/range object and group object belonged to DMZ zone, make sure they are in the same subnet of WAN interface(eg. X18);

4. Select another interface, configure it as DMZ zone/transparent mode, select one of the address objects/groups created in step 3 as Transparent Range and save the settings;

5. Connect a PC to the interface configured in step 4, with proper IP address configured, pass through traffic from DMZ<--->WAN, LAN--->DMZ;

6. Reassign X1 as static WAN mode, retest test step 3 to add Adress Objects/Groups in X1's subnet, verify Transparent Range drop-down list;

GEN7-28861.result:
1. In step 4, FW can show up all the address objects/groups created in step 3 in Transparent Range list;

2. Traffic can pass through in step 5;

3. In step 6, Transparent Range drop-down list contains all the Address Objects/Groups belonged to X1/X18.
